cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Entroly in research, evaluation, or tooling, please cite the software and the exact released version."
title: "Entroly: Context Assurance for AI Agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Entroly Contributors"
version: 1.0.81
date-released: 2026-08-04
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/juyterman1000/entroly"
url: "https://juyterman1000.github.io/entroly/docs/index.html"
abstract: >-
  Entroly is an open-source, local-first Context Assurance layer for AI agents.
  It combines budget-aware evidence selection, recoverable compression,
  content-addressed retrieval, Context Receipts, and evidence verification
  across CLI, SDK, MCP, proxy, wrapper, Rust, Node/WASM, Docker, and Homebrew
  surfaces.
keywords:
  - context assurance
  - context engineering
  - context compression
  - AI agents
  - model context protocol
  - recoverable compression
  - context receipts
  - evidence verification
